    {
      "id": "HNS-02",
      "chapter": "global",
      "anchor": "global-hn-duality",
      "title": "Perpendicular steps and reciprocal normalized volumes",
      "hypotheses": "In addition Λ is self-dual for the nondegenerate Hermitian form h with Gram matrix J, each frame satisfies X_w* J X_w = diag(±1), and conjugation in E is complex conjugation at every infinite place.",
      "statement": "For every saturated M ⊆ Λ, rk M^⊥ + rk M = n and ht(M^⊥)·ht(Λ) = ht(M). Moreover ht(Λ) = 1, M ↦ M^⊥ is an inclusion-reversing involution of the saturated sublattices inverting the heights of successive quotients, (F≤t)^⊥ = F<1/t and (F<t)^⊥ = F≤1/t for t > 0, and in positive rank the largest size of Λ is 1/τ.",
      "definitions": [
        "ht(N) = (2/d)^{f rk N} covol(ρN), so that size(N) = ht(N)^{1/(2f rk N)}.",
        "M^⊥ = Λ ∩ (span M)^⊥ for the form h.",
        "A^∨ is the dual of A over the ring of integers, realized with the dual frames, and N^0 is the annihilator of N."
      ],
      "equations": [
        "global-hn-perp-height"
      ],
